From 42d261b902cfe942f131eaa3b602b9ec390b3ead Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HalalifyMusic <244228683+HalalifyMusic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:15:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(claude): draw Claude Code plugin status lines,
 toasts and prompt band

Claude Code plugins draw UI with $.ui.status, $.ui.toast and an
AbovePrompt ui.render hook. In a headless session the CLI pushes
ui_status / ui_toast / ui_invalidate system messages and draws the band
only when asked with a ui_render control request. T3 dropped all of it.

The Claude query runner now hands those messages and the query's
control-request sender to a ClaudePluginUi service, which keeps a
per-thread snapshot (status lines, latest toast, band tree) and asks
for the band on attach and on each invalidate. Clients subscribe over a
new provider.claude.plugin-ui.subscribe stream; buttons go back through
provider.claude.plugin-ui.press. The web composer draws the band,
status lines and toasts. Nothing is persisted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
