From ac194314449e1fedcdf552a5f4a2a6b4c6bd9173 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HalalifyMusic <244228683+HalalifyMusic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:25:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(claude): draw plugin block art without seams and fit
 the band's width
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Block elements (█ ▀ ▄ ▙ ▟ …) drew as font glyphs, whose anti-aliased edges
striped plugin pixel art. They now draw as painted boxes, full and half
block runs as one box, each overlapping its neighbours by half a pixel.

The band asks plugins for 100 columns instead of 80, so three-column
layouts no longer run into each other, and its font shrinks to fit when
the composer is narrower than that.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
